content.text:
I filed it as **#1622**: https://github.com/raman325/lock_code_manager/issues/1622

It uses the bug-report template and covers:
- what happens: the deleted user's PIN keeps working;
- why it's invisible today;
- how it relates to #1453;
- that the fix depends on the planned coordinator refactor.

The steps say it was found in code review and hasn't been reproduced on hardware yet, so the issue doesn't claim more than we know. The roadmap's priority note now links to it.

The bug-fix implementer is still working on `fix/provider-responses`. The Pyright warnings above come from its in-progress test file, not from committed code. When it finishes, I'll run `/code-review` until a round comes back clean, then open the PR for your review.

